# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Research project .gitignore template.
# Rule of thumb: ignore anything a script can regenerate; keep hand-authored input.
# Tune the discipline-specific block to your solver/method.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Solver runtime artifacts (OpenFOAM example — adapt per discipline) ---
processor*/
postProcessing/
VTK/
dynamicCode/
constant/polyMesh
**/constant/polyMesh/

# Generated OpenFOAM/ParaView marker files
*.OpenFOAM
*.foam

# Generated time directories. Keep the initial-condition directory 0/ tracked.
[1-9]*/
[1-9][0-9]*/
[1-9]*.[0-9]*/
0.[0-9]*/

# Raw sampled-data dumps (bulky; regenerate from cases/ when needed)
*.dat

# --- Logs and local run output ---
log
log.*
*.log
*.out
*.err
*.pid

# --- Regenerable derived artifacts (produced by tools/ and report/scripts/) ---
results/
report/figures/
report/_archive/
*.png
*.csv
*.txt

# Generated Office deliverables (regenerate via report build scripts)
*.docx
*.pptx
*.xlsx

# --- Language / editor caches ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.bak
*~
.#*
.DS_Store

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: ignoring *.png/*.csv/*.txt globally also hides hand-made assets. If you
# keep a tracked figure or dataset, force-add it:  git add -f path/to/keep.png
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
